# Line-ending policy.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS HERE, beyond tidiness: the ai-native-sdlc release pipeline publishes a
# CycloneDX SBOM in which every file carries its own SHA-256, plus a tarball that is meant
# to be byte-reproducible. A checkout that converts LF to CRLF changes those bytes, so the
# SAME content would inventory under a DIFFERENT hash depending on the machine that built
# it. That silently undermines both the "reproducible" claim and any consumer trying to
# verify a hash they were given.
#
# Discovered concretely: the Windows CI cells failed because a test fixture written in text
# mode became CRLF on disk, and its SHA-256 no longer matched the literal the test asserted.
# The test was fixed to write bytes, but the underlying exposure was the repository having
# no line-ending policy at all.

# Normalise text files to LF in the repository, and check them out as LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts whose bytes are hashed, signed, or executed. CRLF here would also break a
# shebang on POSIX, so these are pinned explicitly rather than left to detection.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# Binary types: never translate, never diff as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.tar   binary
